{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:9aedb78658436257","name":"FEG-Series Pilot Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-9aedb78658436257","title":"FEG-Series Pilot Droid","revision":20152,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:18:48Z","sha256":"72bc1a060e44945b8dfffc325f15c3d90c35ca181e08686289b4eb571ae9e511","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20152","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=FEG-Series%20Pilot%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-9aedb78658436257","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["More sophisticated than most automated Pilot Droids, the FEG-Series Pilot Droid from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cybot Galactica"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cybot_Galactica","referenceId":"reference:8d89ff519236e3e2"}," is renowned for its ability to devise creative piloting maneuvers. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cybot Galactica"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cybot_Galactica","referenceId":"reference:8d89ff519236e3e2"}," engineered the FEG-Series to be able to make snap decisions and mimic the creativity of living pilots. The impetus behind this design was that the FEG-Series was intended to serve as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Copilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Copilot","referenceId":"reference:49f5b0e488cfa66c"}," (or even primary ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"},") on ships hauling cargo through dangerous space corridors or guiding stealthy scout craft into hostile territory.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Though most ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transport"}," pilots scoff at the idea of a Pilot Droid being as good as a living pilot, the FEG-Series Pilot Droid is exceptionally good at adapting to rapidly changing circumstances and, in some cases, has outflow living pilots during test runs. That said, a FEG-Series Pilot Droid can't talk its way past Imperial customs or negotiate docking fees with local spaceports as well as seasoned spacers.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Many owners of FEG-Series Pilot Droids use them as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Copilots"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Copilots"}," and intentionally let them go for long periods of time without ",{"tag":"a","children":["Memory Wipes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Memory_Wipes"}," so that they develop personalities. These owners claim that FEG-Series Pilot Droids with developed personalities are even more capable of creative piloting, and some pilots develop long-standing and amicable relationships with their FEG-Series Pilot Droids, treating them more like partners than property. Unfortunately, many of the FEG-Series Pilot Droids allowed to develop their own personalities have become aware of Cybot Galactica's marketing campaign surrounding their model, leading some to adopt a certain arrogance regarding their own piloting skills.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The pirate captain ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rav"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rav","referenceId":"reference:c5abb80ae0de96f3"}," used an FEG-Series Pilot Droid named FEG-13 (\"Feejee 13\") on raids.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["FEG-Series Pilot Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["FEG-Series Pilot Droid Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["2nd-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/2nd-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"}," 1\n"